				<blockquote class="messageText SelectQuoteContainer ugc baseHtml">
					
					<div style="text-align: center"><img src="https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/cover/43a2903edd1fe1cddbe731576da7f455/1900x1900-000000-80-0-0.jpg" class="bbCodeImage LbImage" alt="[​IMG]" data-url="https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/cover/43a2903edd1fe1cddbe731576da7f455/1900x1900-000000-80-0-0.jpg" style=""> <br>
<b><br>
Madonna - American Life: Instrumentals (CDRip) I 16bit / 44.1kHz </b><br>
<br>
<i>American Life</i> is the ninth studio album by American singer <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Madonna</a>. It was released on April 21, 2003, by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maverick_(company)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Maverick</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warner_Records" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Warner Bros. Records</a>. The album, produced by the singer and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirwais_Ahmadza%C3%AF" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Mirwais Ahmadzaï</a>, features references to many parts of American culture. The album is a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Concept_album" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">concept album</a>, with themes panning the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Dream" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">American Dream</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Materialism" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">materialism</a>. These themes reject the reputation Madonna held in the 1980s, earned by her 1984 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Hot_100" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow"><i>Billboard</i> Hot 100</a> number-two hit, "<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Material_Girl" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Material Girl</a>". <i>American Life</i> is a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Folktronica" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">folktronica</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eurodance" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">eurotechno</a> album, influenced by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acoustic_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">acoustic music</a>.<br>
